/-!
# A globally generated twist of a very ample sheaf is very ample

Let `f : X ⟶ Spec k` be a proper scheme over a field, `𝒢` an invertible `𝒪_X`-module generated by
its global sections and `𝒱` an invertible `𝒪_X`-module very ample relative to `f`. Then `𝒢 ⊗ 𝒱` is
very ample relative to `f`.

The source's argument composes `(φ_𝒢, φ_𝒱) : X ⟶ 𝐏^r × 𝐏^m` with the Segre embedding. On the
standard affine charts that argument reads as follows, and that is the form proved here. Very
ampleness of an invertible `ℒ` is clause (4) of [Stacks, Tag 01VR]: the canonical map
`f^* f_* ℒ ⟶ ℒ` is surjective and `r_ℒ : X ⟶ 𝐏(f_* ℒ)` is an immersion, which may be checked on
the charts `X_b ⟶ Spec Sym(f_* ℒ)(W)_{(b)}` at degree-one sections `b` covering `X`. Around a point
`x`, choose a section `c` of `𝒱` whose chart is an immersion (this is the very ampleness of `𝒱`)
and a global section `g` of `𝒢` not vanishing at `x` (global generation). Multiplication by `g`
is a morphism `m : 𝒱 ⟶ 𝒱 ⊗ 𝒢`, and on `X_{g c} ⊆ X_c` the ratios `(g h)/(g c)` are the ratios
`h/c`. Hence the chart of `𝒱` at `c`, restricted to `X_{g c}`, is the chart of `𝒱 ⊗ 𝒢` at `g c`
followed by `Spec` of the ring map `h/c ↦ (g h)/(g c)`. This is the Segre map on these charts.
An immersion that factors this way has an immersion as its first factor ([Stacks, Tag 07RK]).

## Main results

* `Faltings.isRelativelyVeryAmple_tensorModules_of_isGeneratedByGlobalSections`: the tensor
  product of a globally generated invertible sheaf and a very ample invertible sheaf on a proper
  `k`-scheme is very ample.

## Implementation notes

The Segre embedding itself is `Stacks.RelativeSegre.segre`, but the identification of the pull
back of `𝒪(1)` along it with the external tensor product of the twists is not available. The
chartwise form above needs no twist at all, only the ratios of sections, so it is the form
used. The comparison of ratios along `m` is `ratioOf_map`, and the generation of
`Sym(E)(W)_{(c)}` by the ratios `h/c` is `Stacks.RelativeSegre.away_mem_of_ratios`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01VR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01VR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07RK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07RK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01WD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WD)
-/

@[expose] public section

